        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1373568782,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Helichrysum italicum is a tender perennial (USDA Zones 7–10). It is propagated by rooting semi-hardwood cuttings in summer and overwintering in frost-free conditions.",
